 - a clearly different information objective.
 
 This converts accumulated history into actual avoidance of wasted search.
 
+**Implementation:** The novelty guard uses `state/LEARNING_STATE.md` to track resolved frontier cells. When a frontier cell is resolved, the system records:
+
+- Signal class (e.g., "momentum")
+- Parameter values (e.g., lookback periods)
+- Data regime used (synthetic vs real)
+- The verdict (FALSIFIED/TESTED/SUPPORTED)
+
+A new experiment is considered equivalent if it:
+1. Tests the same signal class on the same data regime
+2. Uses parameter values within the previously tested ranges (e.g., lookback 3-20 for momentum)
+3. Has the same diagnostic purpose (e.g., robustness test vs new signal validation)
+
+If the new experiment falls within these equivalence bounds, the system flags it as duplicate and requires justification from the researcher before execution.
+
 ### 3. Measure information gain, not activity
 
